---
/**
 * The markup a rendered guide hands to ReadingGuide's slot, for its story and test: numbered steps, a
 * screenshot with its caption and a note. A component because the story sanitiser drops `aside` from a
 * slot written as a string.
 */
import people from '../../../../../docs/screenshots/member-guide/people.jpg?url';
---

<h1>How to update our website</h1>
<p>
  Words in <strong>bold</strong> are words you will see on the screen.
</p>
<h2 id="add-or-change-a-person">Add or change a person</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Open <strong>People</strong>, then <strong>People</strong>.</li>
  <li>
    Choose the person to change. To add someone new, press the <strong>+</strong> button at the top right
    of the list.
  </li>
  <li>
    Check your work and publish it. The steps are under
    <a href="#check-your-work-and-publish">Check your work and publish</a>.
  </li>
</ol>
<figure>
  <img
    src={people}
    alt="The People list with the + button at its top right"
    width="702"
    height="195"
  />
  <figcaption>The + button is at the top right of the list.</figcaption>
</figure>
<aside>
  <p>Good to know</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Studio saves your work for you as you type. There is no Save button.</li>
    <li>Visitors see your work only after you press <strong>Publish</strong>.</li>
  </ul>
</aside>
<h2 id="check-your-work-and-publish">Check your work and publish</h2>
<h3>Before you publish</h3>
<p>Yoruba words and names have their marks, as in Ẹ káàbọ̀ and Ọjà Balógun.</p>
